   "type": "text",
   "text": "A IS what “like the other projects” means — same Project → epic-milestones → D1–D6 issues shape as GGCE, so all 4 read the same way. Your closed sprints already live in\nscrum/sprints/ (001–012 archived), so nothing is lost by leaving them there. If you want the current sprint visible: add C’s single current-cycle + one “Sprint Log” doc — a small\nbolt-on with no rework. B (100+ historical issues) buys little the vault archive doesn’t already give, and breaks the cross-project convention.",
